fault values are taken from the information provided in the file,
which, if running as root, is created using the built‐in defaults
if it does not exist.  See for more information about After  set‐
ting  any  defaults,  and  then reading values from the following
command line options are processed: Enable user  accounts  to  be
temporary locked/closed.  The operand can be given as to lock the
account  or  to unlock the account.  Set the comment field (also,
for historical reasons known as the GECOS field)  for  the  user.
